    {
      "grid": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 48,
        "h": 12
      },
      "config": {
        "hide_title": false,
        "title": "How to walk DB slowness",
        "content": "## Walk this board top to bottom\nThis is the Elastic path from **DB slowness** to the **app**, the **SQL**, the **trace**, and the **logs**. Default time range is **last 3 days**.\n\n1. **KPIs** \u2014 postgresql client spans lasting **\u22651 s**. If these are empty, the database is not the story.\n2. **Chart** \u2014 which RDS host is producing the slow spans.\n3. **Apps** \u2014 which services called that host.\n4. **SQL** \u2014 `db.query.text` grouped by `FROM` table (search service is the long tail).\n5. **Traces** \u2014 click `trace.id` to open the APM waterfall. Parent work is often an ActiveMQ `EntityDeleted` fan-out, not a user HTTP click.\n6. **Search logs** \u2014 same pods, **`EntityDeleted` only** (DEW fan-out), not Postgres errors. Click `trace.id`.\n7. **webapi errors** \u2014 user-facing API on the same traces (excludes `DuplicateTriggerTimeout` noise).\n8. **Ingress** \u2014 ALB to `apm-classic-stage` queryengine/search, same `trace.id`.\n9. **RDS CPU / queue** \u2014 `apm-classic-stage-rds`. Host CPU is not what explains 10\u201367 minute `SELECT \u2026 count(*) over ()` on `MI_EQUIP000`.\n\n**False lead:** `paf-postgres-dc-test` is a Spring Boot *connector* that restarted 15 Sep 04:52 UTC (CPU 335% of limit during boot). It is not the database, and PAF apps are barely traced to it.\n\n[Example 67-minute span](https://my-observability-project-f2e495.kb.us-west-2.aws.elastic.cloud/s/sre/app/apm/link-to/trace/9a51f6833eb9be520f647e3c8111877c) \u00b7 [AppHub \u2192 Meridium (user hop)](/s/sre/app/dashboards#/view/sre-apphub-meridium-latency) \u00b7 [Alerts](/s/sre/app/observability/alerts)",
        "settings": {
          "open_links_in_new_tab": true
        }
      },
      "id": "db-md",
      "type": "markdown"
    },
